1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,080
Sixty eight percent of the universe
宇宙的百分之六十八，

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:03,010
might not exist.
可能根本不存在。

3
00:00:03,010 --> 00:00:04,580
We're talking about dark energy.
说的是暗能量。

4
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:07,410
This week, a team of mathematicians took a swing at it.
这周，几位数学家冲它挥了一拳。

5
00:00:07,410 --> 00:00:09,480
A new paper says Einstein's own equations
新论文说，爱因斯坦自己的方程

6
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:11,510
might explain the universe without it.
也许不用暗能量就能解释宇宙。

7
00:00:11,510 --> 00:00:12,620
Today's brain teaser:
今天的烧脑问题：

8
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:15,600
can a pencil standing on its tip knock over cosmology?
一支立在笔尖上的铅笔，能推倒整个宇宙学吗？

9
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,030
First, the mystery. The universe is expanding,
先说谜题：宇宙在膨胀，

10
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:20,010
like bread dough rising in an oven.
就像烤箱里发起来的面包。

11
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:21,330
Galaxies are the raisins.
星系是面包里的葡萄干，

12
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:23,420
They all drift apart from each other.
彼此越离越远。

13
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:24,990
Gravity should slow that down,
引力本该让膨胀变慢，

14
00:00:24,990 --> 00:00:27,210
like a ball thrown up slows as it rises.
就像往上扔的球越飞越慢。

15
00:00:27,210 --> 00:00:30,840
But in nineteen ninety eight, astronomers watched distant exploding stars
可是一九九八年，天文学家看遥远的爆炸恒星，

16
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:32,110
and found the opposite.
发现正好相反。

17
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:33,710
The expansion is speeding up.
膨胀在加速。

18
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:35,650
That discovery won a Nobel Prize.
这个发现拿了诺贝尔奖。

19
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:36,970
Imagine throwing a ball up
想象你往上扔个球，

20
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:38,980
and watching it go faster and faster.
它越飞越快。

21
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,250
Something must be pushing.
一定有东西在推。

22
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:42,520
Scientists named that something dark energy.
科学家给它起名叫暗能量。

23
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:45,740
In the standard model, dark energy is about sixty eight percent
按标准模型，暗能量占宇宙的

24
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:47,290
of everything in the cosmos.
大约百分之六十八。

25
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:48,190
And nobody knows
可它到底是什么，

26
00:00:48,190 --> 00:00:49,430
what it actually is.
没人知道。

27
00:00:49,430 --> 00:00:51,010
Twist one: the idea is old.
反转一：这个点子很老了。

28
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:54,160
Einstein added a similar term in nineteen seventeen.
爱因斯坦一九一七年就加过类似的一项。

29
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:56,520
He reportedly called it his biggest blunder.
据说他后来称之为一生最大的错误。

30
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:57,600
Then it came back.
结果它又回来了。

31
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:01,270
The new paper comes from UC Davis and University College London,
新论文来自加州大学戴维斯分校和伦敦大学学院，

32
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:02,940
in a Royal Society journal.
发表在英国皇家学会的期刊上。

33
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:05,600
Their target is the standard model of the cosmos,
它瞄准的是宇宙的标准模型，

34
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,570
the one with dark energy built in.
就是自带暗能量的那个。

35
00:01:07,570 --> 00:01:08,430
Here's the pencil.
来看这支铅笔。

36
00:01:08,430 --> 00:01:10,460
You can balance it perfectly on its tip.
你可以让它完美地立在笔尖上。

37
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:12,730
Mathematically, that's a real solution.
数学上，这是个真解：

38
00:01:12,730 --> 00:01:14,120
All the forces cancel.
所有的力正好抵消。

39
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:15,730
But one tiny breath of air,
可只要一丝风，

40
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:16,620
and it falls.
它就倒了。

41
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:18,260
Twist two, the surprising one:
反转二，最意外：

42
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:21,120
they say our model of the universe is that pencil.
他们说，我们的宇宙模型就是这支铅笔。

43
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:22,470
They found it's unstable.
他们算出它不稳定：

44
00:01:22,470 --> 00:01:25,350
Tiny ripples on huge scales grow instead of fading.
超大尺度上的小涟漪会长大，而不是消失。

45
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:26,560
The lead author argues
论文作者认为，

46
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:29,090
that nature doesn't pick unstable solutions.
不稳定的解，大自然不会选。

47
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:31,970
So what if the universe already slid off the balance point?
那如果宇宙早就从平衡点滑开了呢？

48
00:01:31,970 --> 00:01:34,910
In their picture, that slide could look like acceleration.
在他们的图景里，这一滑，看起来就像加速。

49
00:01:34,910 --> 00:01:35,770
And it would need
而且，

50
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:37,000
no dark energy at all.
根本不需要暗能量。

51
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,920
Twist three: this paper isn't alone.
反转三：怀疑暗能量的不只这篇论文。

52
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:43,580
Last year, a giant galaxy survey called DESI hinted that dark energy may be changing.
去年，巨型星系巡天DESI暗示，暗能量可能在变。

53
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:44,470
If it can change,
如果它会变，

54
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:46,880
maybe it was never a constant to begin with.
它也许从来就不是一个常数。

55
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:48,950
Fine print: so far this is pure math.
友情提示：目前这还是纯数学，

56
00:01:48,950 --> 00:01:51,760
Nobody has tested it against telescope data yet.
还没拿望远镜的数据检验过。

57
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:54,170
And many cosmologists still think dark energy
很多宇宙学家仍然认为，

58
00:01:54,170 --> 00:01:56,440
is the best explanation for what we see.
暗能量是对观测最好的解释。

59
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:59,100
A new idea has to predict something we can measure.
新想法得做出能测量的预言，

60
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:00,320
That's the next step.
这才是下一步。

61
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:03,020
So, can a pencil on its tip knock over cosmology?
所以，笔尖上的铅笔能推倒宇宙学吗？

62
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:05,170
Maybe, if the universe is the pencil.
也许能，如果宇宙就是那支铅笔。

63
00:02:05,170 --> 00:02:06,860
Sixty eight percent of everything
宇宙的百分之六十八，

64
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:08,470
is riding on a balancing act.
押在一个平衡上。

65
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:10,140
Either dark energy is real,
要么暗能量是真的，

66
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:11,310
and deeply weird.
而且怪得要命。

67
00:02:11,310 --> 00:02:12,840
Or our best map of the cosmos
要么我们最好的宇宙地图，

68
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:15,240
has been standing on its tip all along.
一直都立在笔尖上。

